  "description": "Two-Bedroom Apartments at Quayside Quarter, Dublin Docklands\n\nDiscover world-class customer service when you rent a two-bedroom apartment at Quayside Quarter in the heart of Dublin. These spacious apartments are designed for renters looking for a new standard of city living.\n\nTwo-bedroom apartments at Quayside Quarter range from approximately 796 to 1,076 sq. ft. and are pet friendly.\n\nApartments are beautifully furnished, with the living experience extending beyond your front door to a range of resident amenity spaces and services, including an onsite gym, Residents' Lounge, sky gardens, 24/7 concierge and more.\n\nQuayside Quarter Resident Amenities\n\nResidents at Quayside Quarter have access to a range of amenities, facilities and services, including:\n\n- 24/7 concierge\n- Resident gym\n- Pet-friendly development\n- 24/7 onsite maintenance and management\n- Private gym\n- Co-working spaces\n- Residents' Lounge\n- Communal roof terrace areas\n- Secure bike storage\n- Electric car charging\n- Parking available by separate negotiation\n- Dry cleaning services\n- Landscaped gardens\n\nFeatured Top-Floor Apartment\n\nThis top-floor apartment features a wrap-around southwest-facing balcony with views across Dublin City. Residents of this apartment also have direct access to a rooftop garden terrace, providing outdoor space for enjoying morning sunrises and evening sunsets.\n\nThe apartment is just under 1,000 sq. ft. and combines spacious accommodation with extensive city views.\n\nQuayside Quarter Development\n\nLocated at the forefront of Dublin Docklands and consisting of 268 premium apartments, Quayside Quarter sets a new standard for rented apartment living in the city.\n\nResidents benefit from a professional service managed by Greystar, as well as access to quality apartments and a range of additional resident benefits.\n\nAll apartments are pet friendly, and residents can choose from furnished or unfurnished options across an array of floorplans, with some apartments offering waterfront views.\n\nResidents' Lounge, Co-working Spaces and Private Gym\n\nDesigned to refine the work-life balance, the Residents' Lounge is an elegant and considered space created to meet residents' needs. It features hot desks, meeting spaces and a games area for downtime, providing a space made for collaborators.\n\nThe private gym is flooded with natural light and features a raw industrial aesthetic.\n\nDesign and Architecture\n\nThe development draws its inspiration from the fabric of Dublin and the rich industrial heritage of the Docklands, infused with contemporary Scandinavian architectural accents and Brooklyn loft-style design.\n\nProperty Features\n\nProperty features include:\n\n- Parking\n- Central heating\n- Cable television\n- Hotpoint appliances\n- Dishwasher\n- Microwave\n- Pets allowed\n- Wheelchair access\n- Internet\n- Garden, patio or balcony\n- Concierge\n- Gym\n- Residents' Lounge\n- Community events\n- Co-working space\n- Laundry\n\nLocation and Transport\n\nQuayside Quarter is conveniently located only 5 minutes from the Docklands rapid rail station (DART) and directly next to the Spencer Dock light rail station (LUAS).\n\nFrom Quayside Quarter, Point Square can be reached in approximately 1 minute on foot, while offices in the IFSC are approximately 4 minutes away on foot. Dublin Airport is approximately 20 minutes away by taxi.\n\nThe surrounding neighbourhood draws its inspiration from the fabric of Dublin and the rich industrial heritage of the Docklands, with contemporary Scandinavian architectural accents and Brooklyn loft-style design.\n\nCurated wild landscapes sit alongside bustling streets with restaurants, cafés and stores. A riverfront boutique hotel anchors the area, contributing to a vibrant new neighbourhood.\n\nContact Quayside Quarter\n\nTo contact a member of the Quayside Quarter site team, email team@qquarter.com or call 01 5395960.\n\nRental Information\n\nPlease note that multiple property types are available within the Quayside Quarter development. The rent advertised on individual property advertisements represents the starting rent for those property types.\n\nRent varies throughout the development depending on different aspects of each property type. Not all available properties and rents are listed.",
